---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Priyansh Sarvaiya and Signal in the Context."
>
  <section class="page-heading">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Priyansh Sarvaiya</h1>
      <p>
        Computing Science student at Simon Fraser University, interested in
        AI/ML, LLMs, NLP, world models, long-context reasoning, and AGI.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section compact">
    <div class="container narrow prose-page">
      <p>
        I use this site as a public research notebook: a place for paper
        reviews, technical explainers, experiment writeups, and notes on the
        questions that keep coming up while studying modern AI systems.
      </p>
      <p>
        My current focus is language model reasoning under imperfect context.
        In practical settings, models rarely receive clean textbook prompts.
        They receive long histories, irrelevant details, stale instructions,
        partial evidence, and sometimes misleading context. I am interested in
        how that extra information changes a model's ability to identify the
        right signal and reason from it.
      </p>
      <p>
        More broadly, I am interested in the connection between language,
        representation learning, planning, and world models. I want to
        understand what current LLMs can already do, where they break, and what
        kinds of architectures, training signals, and evaluations might be
        needed for more reliable intelligent systems.
      </p>
      <p>
        The writing here is meant to stay clear and useful. Some posts are
        polished essays, some are research notes, and some are explanations
        written to make a difficult idea easier to reason about.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
